WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.364 --> 00:00:03.506
- [Narrator] Nestled in the
side of the Yoro Mountains,

00:00:03.506 --> 00:00:06.024
the Site of Reversible Destiny in Japan

00:00:06.024 --> 00:00:07.672
is an experience park

00:00:07.672 --> 00:00:10.839
where guests encounter the unexpected.

00:00:17.055 --> 00:00:20.331
The park was designed by
artists Shusaku Arakawa

00:00:20.331 --> 00:00:23.371
and Madeline Gins, and
consists of sculptures,

00:00:23.371 --> 00:00:27.119
pavilions and constantly
changing terrains.

00:00:27.119 --> 00:00:30.331
There is an intricate network of 148 paths

00:00:30.331 --> 00:00:32.747
and 24 types of plants that emphasize

00:00:32.747 --> 00:00:35.691
the changing of the season,
such as cherry blossoms

00:00:35.691 --> 00:00:40.665
in the springtime and vibrant
autumn leaves in the fall.

00:00:40.665 --> 00:00:42.107
Some of the attractions include

00:00:42.107 --> 00:00:43.755
The Critical Resemblance House,

00:00:43.755 --> 00:00:45.915
which has a map of Gifu Prefecture,

00:00:45.915 --> 00:00:49.248
a region of central Japan, as a rooftop,

00:00:50.151 --> 00:00:51.947
and the Reversible Destiny office

00:00:51.947 --> 00:00:55.179
that contains an uneven
pastel-colored maze

00:00:55.179 --> 00:00:59.505
and a ceiling that mirrors
the design of the floor.

00:00:59.505 --> 00:01:01.459
Visitors are encouraged
to explore the site

00:01:01.459 --> 00:01:05.155
with the mindset of a
child, to climb, be curious,

00:01:05.155 --> 00:01:09.028
and discover different visual perceptions.

00:01:09.028 --> 00:01:11.462
But because of slanting
angles, steep hills,

00:01:11.462 --> 00:01:14.803
and narrow pathways, the
Site of Reversible Destiny

00:01:14.803 --> 00:01:18.970
offers optional helmets to
ensure a safe excursion.

